    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nI love to have the preview column to see the content of a file before committing to get inside of it.\r\n\r\nThe issue is, I find the fact that the cursor is on the **next to last** column, and not the last column itself, pretty unintuitive, and find myself looking at the wrong column all the time when navigating. \r\n\r\nI could make the width of the preview column smaller, but it doesn't help much visually, while reducing the effectiveness of the preview column. \r\n\r\nTo me personally the best solution would be pretty simple: somehow highlight the focus column, not only with width change, but perhaps also with border color change. For example it would be lovely if the border color of the focus column is tokyonight's orange \r\n<img width=\"1353\" alt=\"SCR-20240516-tpit\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/113684938/c10189d5-add8-4e1e-8524-c0b8fbf7ed20\">\r\n\r\n\r\nAnother idea would be to give \"inactive columns\" a backdrop effect where the syntax highlight colors are disabled (similar to how [flash](https://github.com/folke/flash.nvim) does it). \"Inactive columns\" here refer to all the columns that are not focus column or preview column. \r\n<img width=\"1358\" alt=\"SCR-20240516-tqnw\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/113684938/94ad7e08-d209-48e1-a70d-f952f06d68c4\">\r\n\r\nIt would make my life so much easier if one of these could be implemented or configurable somehow. \r\n\r\nThank you so much for an awesome plugin!",
